<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernest I, Duke of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1784–1844</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernest I was Duke of Saxe-Coburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saalfeld">Saalfeld</a> from 1806 and, after the Ernestine redistribution of 1826, the first Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a>. He gained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> Principality of Lichtenberg in 1816 but sold it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1834. He was the father of Prince Albert, husband of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/queen-victoria">Queen Victoria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-coburg-and-gotha.jpg" alt="Ernest I, Duke of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Dawe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernst_I,_Duke_of_Saxe-Coburg_and_Gotha_-_Dawe_1818-19.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
